    a: 'WorldFreightHub Europe route data records roughly 30 days by sea from Shanghai, Ningbo-Zhoushan or Shenzhen to Gdańsk on the current Cape-of-Good-Hope routing, within a 25–45 day planning range. The Red Sea reroute adds about +10–14 days versus the pre-crisis Suez routing (MEDIUM confidence, because these are planning estimates, not carrier promises). New Silk Road rail into Małaszewicze runs roughly 18–22 days, but the final Central-Eastern Europe connection adds time. No verified Poland air transit is published in the snapshot — request that from your carrier.',
