    q: 'How does Poland’s 23% VAT compound on imports?',
    a: 'Poland applies the EU’s second-highest standard VAT rate at 23%, behind only Hungary’s 27%. Import VAT is charged on the duty-inclusive value, so the statutory calculation is (CIF + duty) × 1.23 — duty first, then 23% VAT on top of duty and CIF together. That compounding makes the HS code the first cost decision: a higher duty line is magnified by the 23% VAT on the higher duty-inclusive base.',
