    q: 'What is the difference between FCL and LCL for China to Poland?',
    a: 'FCL gives you exclusive use of a 20GP, 40GP or 40HQ and is usually the fit for large or heavy loads, priced per container. LCL consolidates your cargo with other importers and is priced per cubic metre. Illustratively, at a midpoint 20ft rate of $3,000 and LCL of $105/CBM, the break-even is about 29 CBM; below that LCL is usually cheaper, above it FCL starts to win. Request quotes on both sides of the split before deciding.',
