    q: 'How do demurrage and detention differ in Poland?',
    a: 'Demurrage is the charge the terminal applies when import cargo stays in the port beyond the allowed free time after discharge. Detention is the charge the ocean carrier (or rail operator) applies when the container is kept beyond the equipment free time after collection. They are two separate clocks with two separate payees. Polish free-time periods and per-day rates are not published in the verified snapshot — confirm both allowances in writing before booking and file the declaration promptly so neither clock runs.',
